  "notes": "Composed of {止|し} (to stop) and {血|けつ} (blood). An essential first aid term. Also functions as a する verb: {止血|しけつ}する (to stop the bleeding).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {止血|しけつ}する — to stop the bleeding\n- {止血|しけつ}{帯|たい} — tourniquet\n- {止血|しけつ}{剤|ざい} — hemostatic agent, styptic\n- {止血|しけつ}{処置|しょち} — hemostatic treatment\n\nUSAGE:\nAppears in first aid instructions, medical discussions, and emergency situations. In first aid, the basic method is {直接|ちょくせつ}{圧迫|あっぱく}{止血|しけつ}{法|ほう} (direct pressure hemostasis) — pressing firmly on the wound.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {出血|しゅっけつ} — bleeding, hemorrhage\n- {流血|りゅうけつ} — bloodshed; more dramatic and figurative\n- {輸血|ゆけつ} — blood transfusion",
